 About: Ports                                                         
   PORT            The number other programs connect to. A port can   
                   only have one listener per address, so "address    
                   already in use" means something here already has   
                   it: search for the port (/) to see what.           
   PROTO           TCP for connections (web servers, databases, SSH). 
                   UDP for messages without a connection (DNS,        
                   discovery, games, video calls).                    
   ADDRESS         Where it listens. 0.0.0.0 or :: means every        
                   network interface, so other machines can reach it  
                   unless a firewall blocks it. 127.0.0.1 or ::1      
                   means this machine only.                           
   PID / PROCESS   The process that owns the socket. Enter goes to it 
